IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Profession Act 2006 (ACT), Part 3.2 (costs disclosure and assessment) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR); the
-- daydate library is not imported. A period "after the day" something happens is counted from the next day, so the
-- last day of "not later than 90 days after the day" a bill is given is the bill day plus 90.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Legal Profession Act 2006 (ACT), Part 3.2`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a number of days after a day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` `the count` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `the count`)

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- The later of two days.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF `the first` `falls before` `the second` THEN `the second` ELSE `the first`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4) EQUALS 0
    AND (    (NOT ((y MODULO 100) EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400) EQUALS 0)

-- "12 months after the day" (s 294A (5)): the same day of the month a year later; from 29 February to a year with no
-- 29 February, 28 February (fork F9 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`12 months after` `the day` MEANS
    IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
        AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
        AND (NOT (`a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
